/** @page tokenizer_vocabguide Vocabulary Access

    @tableofcontents

    @code{.py}
# Get vocabulary size
printf("Vocab size: %d\n", tok.getVocabSize());

# Look up individual tokens
printf("hello -> %d\n", tok.tokenToId("hello"));
printf("7592 -> %s\n", tok.idToToken(7592));

# Get the full vocabulary as a hash
hash<string, int> vocab = tok.getVocab();
printf("Total entries: %d\n", vocab.size());

# Get the pad token ID (auto-detected from [PAD] or <pad>)
printf("Pad token ID: %d\n", tok.getPadTokenId());
    @endcode

    Text and tokens are kept whole, including any NUL characters.  A token with a NUL character (for example, an
    added token) cannot be a hash key, so @ref Qore::Tokenizer::HFTokenizer::getVocab() "getVocab()" raises
    \c HASH-KEY-ERROR when the vocabulary has one; look such a token up with
    @ref Qore::Tokenizer::HFTokenizer::tokenToId() "tokenToId()" and
    @ref Qore::Tokenizer::HFTokenizer::idToToken() "idToToken()" instead.
*/
